From 191a5814c5274bfba7dd010d0e3995b17914f243 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 17:50:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/amd/display: HDMI 3D: frame packing keeps its timing
 beside its 2D twin

create_stream_for_sink() doubles the timing of a frame packed mode in
the crtc_ fields of its copy of the mode (drm_mode_set_crtcinfo() with
CRTC_STEREO_DOUBLE). The other fields stay those of the 2D twin, which
is how DRM describes a 3D mode. Two places further down compare those
other fields with a mode of the sink and, when they match, take the
timing from elsewhere:

- decide_crtc_timing_for_drm_display_mode() copies the crtc_ fields of
  the preferred mode over those of the mode when clock, htotal and
  vtotal match, as they do when the preferred mode is the 2D twin;
- fill_stream_properties_from_drm_display_mode() takes the timing from
  the fields that are not crtc_ ones when is_freesync_video_mode() says
  that the mode is the highest refresh rate mode of the preferred size,
  or one derived from it. For the frame packed twin of that mode it says
  so, whatever amdgpu.freesync_video is.

Either one puts the plain timing of the 2D twin on the wire, under a
vendor InfoFrame that says frame packing and with the doubled frame of
the stream scaled into it. It takes a sink whose preferred mode has a
frame packed twin: 720p60 or 720p50 frame packing on a display that is
720p native at that rate, 1080p24 on one that prefers 1080p24, 1080p60
where a sink offers that. The reports about these patches (1080p24, on a
4K projector) meet neither.

Frame packing now skips both. It keeps the timing that was doubled, is
never replaced by a FreeSync video mode, and its stream does not take
the VIC and the sync polarities of the old stream (preferred_refresh
stays 0, as when the sink has no preferred mode). Side-by-side half and
top-and-bottom are left alone: their timing is the one of the 2D twin,
so both places give them what they give the twin.

A mode that is not frame packing, or is on a connector that does not
allow 3D, takes the branches it took.

Not covered: with amdgpu.freesync_video=1 (off by default)
dm_update_crtc_state() can keep the old stream when the mode changes
within one FreeSync video family; that code knows nothing about 3D.
cinema-ONE's own change to decide_crtc_timing_for_drm_display_mode()
(their 0107: the sync positions are compared too, for 4096x2160 against
3840x2160) is not taken here: it changes what 2D modes get, and it does
not help this case, where every field of the twin matches.

Checked: compiled with the configuration and the compiler of the image;
both places, by running these functions on the build host with 720p60
frame packing against a preferred 720p60 (before: 1280x720 in 750 lines
at 74.25 MHz; now: 1280x1470 in 1500 lines at 148.5 MHz). Not run on
hardware and never seen on a 3D display.
---
 .../gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm.c    | 16 ++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm.c
index de55dbf..19ffb91 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm.c
@@ -7214,7 +7214,12 @@ static void fill_stream_properties_from_drm_display_mode(
 		timing_out->hdmi_vic = hv_frame.vic;
 	}
 
-	if (aconnector && is_freesync_video_mode(mode_in, aconnector)) {
+	/*
+	 * Not for frame packing: the timing the mode has before the CRTC adjustments is
+	 * the one of its 2D twin, and the doubled one is in the crtc_ fields.
+	 */
+	if (aconnector && is_freesync_video_mode(mode_in, aconnector) &&
+	    amdgpu_dm_stereo_layout(connector, mode_in) != DRM_MODE_FLAG_3D_FRAME_PACKING) {
 		timing_out->h_addressable = mode_in->hdisplay;
 		timing_out->h_total = mode_in->htotal;
 		timing_out->h_sync_width = mode_in->hsync_end - mode_in->hsync_start;
@@ -8217,7 +8222,14 @@ create_stream_for_sink(struct drm_connector *connector,
 		 */
 		drm_dbg_driver(dev, "No preferred mode found\n");
 	} else if (aconnector) {
+		/*
+		 * Frame packing keeps the doubled timing it was given above. Its clock and
+		 * its totals, as the mode has them, are those of its 2D twin: where that twin
+		 * is the native mode, or the base of the FreeSync video modes, the timing of
+		 * the twin would be taken instead.
+		 */
 		recalculate_timing = amdgpu_freesync_vid_mode &&
+				 stereo != DRM_MODE_FLAG_3D_FRAME_PACKING &&
 				 is_freesync_video_mode(&mode, aconnector);
 		if (recalculate_timing) {
 			freesync_mode = get_highest_refresh_rate_mode(aconnector, false);
@@ -8225,7 +8237,7 @@ create_stream_for_sink(struct drm_connector *connector,
 			saved_mode.picture_aspect_ratio = mode.picture_aspect_ratio;
 			drm_mode_copy(&mode, freesync_mode);
 			mode.picture_aspect_ratio = saved_mode.picture_aspect_ratio;
-		} else {
+		} else if (stereo != DRM_MODE_FLAG_3D_FRAME_PACKING) {
 			decide_crtc_timing_for_drm_display_mode(
 					&mode, preferred_mode, scale);
 
